--- a/QUOTA_RETRY_V7_0_81.md	1970-01-01 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
+++ b/QUOTA_RETRY_V7_0_81.md	2026-10-22 11:56:03.106030378 +0000
@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+# AutoVideo 7.0.81 — Gemini daily limit stops the run at once
+
+Update from 7.0.80 with `python3 ../AutoVideoAI-v7.0.81/tools/update_v780_to_v781.py . --apply`
+(dry run first without `--apply`; stop the dashboard before applying).
+
+## What happened
+
+The error was `HTTP 429 … Rate limit exceeded for model gemini-3.8-flash-tts (limit: 10 requests per day on Free Tier)`.
+
+- That is a **daily** limit, counted per Google Cloud project and per model. Google resets it at midnight Pacific time.
+- 7.0.80 retried every 429 three times. Each retry is a counted request, so one exhausted daily quota cost three
+  requests per failing part. This was a bug in 7.0.80.
+- A narration is sent in parts of up to 1200 characters, and each language is its own set of requests. A three-language
+  batch can need more than 10 requests before any retry.
+
+## What changed
+
+- `engine/audio/tts.py`
+  - A 429 whose body says "per day" raises `GeminiQuotaExceeded` immediately. No retry is sent.
+  - A per-minute 429 waits 65 seconds before the next attempt (up to 3 attempts), because a shorter wait hits the same window.
+  - The error states how many parts are saved. Saved parts are kept in `<narration>.parts/`, so the next run continues from the
+    first unsaved part and does not resend finished parts.
+  - For Odia, a quota error is reported as a quota error, not as a missing native voice file.
+  - In the auto chain, a quota error on `gemini` still falls back to `gemini-lite`. That model has its own daily limit.
+- `tests/test_v781_quota_retry.py`: five tests (daily limit sent once; per-minute wait then retry; partial run resumes with
+  only the unsaved parts; Odia quota message; other 400 errors still fail at once).
+
+## Options to get more Gemini TTS capacity
+
+1. **Do not add several Google accounts or keys to get around the limit.** Limits are per project, so extra keys in the same
+   project add nothing. Using several accounts to get past a quota is likely a breach of Google's terms. Keep to one account.
+2. **Link billing to the project (Tier 1) and request a higher TTS limit.** Google's rate-limit page shows the live limit per project in Google AI Studio. Third-party reports from October 2026 say the TTS daily limit
+   stayed at 100 on Tier 1 until an increase was requested, so check the limit shown in Google AI Studio after linking billing. Those reports say increases are requested through Google's application form.
+3. **Choose `gemini-lite` in the TTS setting** when `gemini` is exhausted. It has its own daily limit. Check the Odia voice
+   quality on a short test before relying on it.
+4. **Sarvam Bulbul v3 supports Odia (`od-IN`).** It is a separate API with its own key and pricing, and it would need a new
+   provider in the code. Not implemented in 7.0.81.
+5. **Import a native Odia voice file.** Still not available per language (see 7.0.80 notes).
+
+## Not verified
+
+- Whether a 429 for the daily limit also counts against the quota. It was assumed, and sending no retries is safe either way.
+- Live Gemini behaviour from the build sandbox. The 429 and retry paths are tested with a fake server.
